WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.957
Reconnaissance is the information-gathering stage that may happen before visible activity inside the organization.

2
00:00:06.107 --> 00:00:11.639
A defender may never see all of it, which is why preparation matters.

3
00:00:11.789 --> 00:00:20.300
The defensive question is not how to perform reconnaissance; it is what useful information the organization is exposing and how

4
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.650
that exposure can be reduced.

5
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:28.757
Public-facing systems, stale DNS records, forgotten test services, exposed contact information, unmanaged cloud assets,

6
00:00:28.907 --> 00:00:32.312
and vague ownership all make later analysis harder.

7
00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:39.270
Good defensive preparation starts with asset inventory, ownership records, external exposure review, patch and configuration hygiene,

8
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.101
and monitoring for unusual probing against systems the organization cares about.

9
00:00:44.251 --> 00:00:52.762
Analysts should also understand what normal internet noise looks like so they can distinguish routine scanning from activity that deserves

10
00:00:52.912 --> 00:00:55.112
closer review.

11
00:00:55.262 --> 00:00:59.943
Reconnaissance is an early-stage concept, but the defensive work is ongoing.

12
00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:08.603
Keep inventories current, remove unnecessary exposure, validate who owns internet-facing services, and make sure logs exist before an incident begins.

13
00:01:08.753 --> 00:01:15.562
When later evidence appears, that preparation helps the team answer practical questions quickly: what was exposed,

14
00:01:15.712 --> 00:01:20.393
what changed, what was targeted, and which controls were in place.

15
00:01:20.543 --> 00:01:23.947
Preparation also makes later incident notes more reliable.

16
00:01:24.097 --> 00:01:31.331
If the team already knows which assets are exposed, who owns them, and which logs are available,

17
00:01:31.481 --> 00:01:39.140
analysts spend less time reconstructing basic context and more time understanding whether the current activity represents meaningful risk.
